Connecting Lidar.

1. Download lidar software from https://www.livoxtech.com/mid-360/downloads (steps given in user manual)
	1. disable firewall: sudo ufw disable
	2. Set the static IP manually: IP address 192.168.2.1, subnet mask 255.255.255.0, gateway: 192.168.1.1 

	3. /Downloads/LivoxViewer2 for Ubuntu v2.3.0$ ./LivoxViewer2.sh 

	The host ip and lidar ip were otained from the prints of above program

2. Install Livox-SDK2 and run the sample script
	https://github.com/Livox-SDK/Livox-SDK2/tree/master
	Configure the ip in config file in samples/livox_lidar_quick_start/mid360_config.json
	then run: cd samples/livox_lidar_quick_start && ./livox_lidar_quick_start ../../../samples/livox_lidar_quick_start/[config file]


3. Clone the livox ros2 driver. 
	Change the config file
	LAunch the rviz launch file in livox_ros2_driver
	
4. Currently Vinebot uses rtabmap for mapping and localization. It uses 3D camera. Its launch files are launched from the roboteq_control/bringup_vinesalm.launch in ros1


